function ignore value:
    replacement:
        @intrinsic("discard", value)

function return value:
    replacement:
        @intrinsic("return", value)

[an|] integer means: @intrinsic("type", "int")

fixed value means: @intrinsic("fix", value)

an array means: @intrinsic("array")

[an|] array of {fixed integer:length} items means: @intrinsic("array", length)

[an|] array as long as value means: @intrinsic("array", @intrinsic("type extent", value, 0))

the arrays {an array:left} and {an array as long as left:right} have equal length means: 1

to get the arrays left and right have equal length:
    ignore left
    ignore right
    return 0

ignore @intrinsic(
    "variadic call",
    "libc",
    "printf",
    an integer,
    1,
    "%d %d %d\n",
    the arrays [1, 2] and [3.0, 4.0] have equal length,
    the arrays [1, 2] and [3, 4, 5] have equal length,
    @intrinsic("type extent", [6, 7, 8, 9], 0)
)
